import SwiftUI
import KwipMLCore

enum OCRLessonContent {
    static let objective="This canvas reads three synthetic scanned images: an invoice, a contract and a support request. Their words are pixels, not a text column yet. Optical character recognition (OCR) finds text regions and recognizes the words so existing data tools can use them.\n\n- **File Input** captures the selected images.\n- **Prepare media** keeps their geometry and explicitly prepares RGB pixels.\n- **Extract text** returns Documents and Regions tables.\n- **View** lets you inspect text and its source, without running recognition again.\n\nThis practice reads text; it does not train a model or prove document understanding."
    static let terms="- **Region:** a detected piece of printed text and its four source-image corners.\n- **Confidence:** the recognizer's score, not a guarantee that the words are correct.\n- **Document:** the original file, including its ordered pages/frames when grouped.\n- **Model pack:** separately downloaded, pinned detector and recognizer weights."
    static let steps=[
        "Open Settings → Models & assets → Optional OCR model packs. Review English OCR and download it once. The pack is optional and is not installed when the app is first opened. Its source, size and integrity pins are fixed; recognition does not download files. After installation you can use this practice offline. Missing or changed weights produce an actionable failure rather than a hidden download.",
        "Select [Read synthetic scans](kwip-node://data/scans), then [Prepare OCR images](kwip-node://data/pixels). File Input captures the three supplied PNGs. Prepare media outputs an image, keeps its source and records the coordinate transform. Compare its explicit RGB and alpha policies. Keep dimensions for this first run; resizing small text can remove detail. Apply changes before running.",
        "Select [Read printed text](kwip-node://data/ocr). Keep the initial settings for these synthetic scans, then Run Flow.\n\n- **Detection maximum side** caps the detector image in pixels; a larger cap alone does not enlarge a smaller image.\n- **Detection magnification** enlarges the detector input up to that cap. It can help find small text but cannot recover missing source detail.\n- **Review below confidence** flags recognized regions for checking. It does not improve recognition or measure accuracy.\n\nDocuments contains one text row per original file. Regions contains the recognized pieces, confidence scores and four corners in source-image pixels. No-text pages remain with a noText status. A failed read is different from a blank page; inspect component Diagnostics if execution fails.",
        "Open [Inspect text regions](kwip-node://data/regions). Use the normal table search, sort and paging controls. Open source_image to view the captured image and selectable boxes. The detail view labels that its overlays cover the current table page. Confidence review flags keep the exact recognized text; they do not remove words or silently correct them. Image zoom and Fit affect display only.",
        "Open [Inspect document text](kwip-node://data/documents). Check INVOICE 42 against the image, then inspect the other two documents. Save and reopen the project; History reads retained text/source evidence without OCR or a download. Uncaptured source media is shown as unavailable. To classify scans, join explicit labels to Documents, group/split original documents before fitting text features, then follow Classify private documents. Keep all pages of one document in one population.",
        "Try a copy of the workflow with File Input's PDF content set explicitly to Page images, then choose page selection and render DPI. Embedded text remains a separate reader choice, with no automatic OCR fallback. Rendering and recognition obey pixel, page, text and region bounds; an allowance failure is not a successful truncated result. Export scalar text/coordinates through Table Output. Handwriting, complex layouts and OCR fine-tuning are not qualified by this practice."
    ]
    static let boundary="This editable practice is unscored. OCR does not infer invoice fields, reconstruct semantic tables or establish clinical accuracy. Original source access, optional model acquisition and run-detail capture are separate controls. Extracted text can contain private data. Whole-workflow OCR Code export is explicitly unavailable until verified pack capture is portable; native saved workflows and scalar Table Output remain available. Direct OCR input is qualified for document classification, while neural-network Train requires exporting the Documents table first."
}
struct OCRLearningView:View {
    @ObservedObject var store:WorkspaceStore
    var body:some View {Button("Open OCR practice"){_=store.loadComponentWorkflowExample(OCRPracticeExample.exampleID,device:"cpu")}.buttonStyle(FlatButtonStyle()).disabled(store.isBusy)}
}
